# Python dev dependencies for the binding CI (build + test). Compiled to a
# hash-locked ci-dev.txt with:
#   uv pip compile --generate-hashes --universal --python-version 3.9 \
#     .github/requirements/ci-dev.in -o .github/requirements/ci-dev.txt
# --universal with the oldest interpreter the Python job runs, so one lock
# carries markers for 3.9 through 3.13 instead of resolving for whichever
# Python compiled it.
# The screener's Python tests only build the extension and parse JSON reports,
# so no array/math dependency (numpy) is needed — one lockfile covers py39-py313.
maturin
pytest
# The Python job's oldest interpreter is 3.9; iniconfig 2.2+ requires 3.10.
iniconfig<2.2
# pytest resolves to 9.x on 3.10+ and to 8.4.2 on 3.9, which is below the fix
# for GHSA-6w46-j5rx-g56g (vulnerable tmpdir handling; the fix requires 3.10).
# Not reachable here: no test uses tmp_path or tmpdir, and the runner is a
# single-user VM. The Dependabot alert on the 3.9 line is dismissed as not used.
